# What the API refuses, and with which status. Every error is RFC 9457 Problem Details
# (application/problem+json) with a stable `type` URN, whichever layer answered (ADR 0007).
# Environment and token refresh: see orders.http (`make http-env`).

### Setup: alice creates an order the requests below refer to
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "currency": "EUR", "items": [ { "sku": "ABC-123", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 1999 } ] }

> {% client.global.set("aliceOrderId", response.body.id); %}

# --- Authentication: one generic 401 from the gateway, whatever is wrong (ADR 0003) ---

### 401: no token at all (the gateway answers without calling the authorizer)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{aliceOrderId}}

### 401: not a bearer token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{aliceOrderId}}
Authorization: Basic YWxpY2U6c2VjcmV0

### 401: a bearer value that isn't a JWT
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{aliceOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer not-a-token

# --- Authorization: 403 before any data is read, 404 for orders the caller may not see (ADR 0001) ---

### 403: nobody holds a valid token but no recognised role
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{aliceOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{nobodyToken}}

### 404: bob (USER) asks for alice's order; it looks exactly like one that doesn't exist
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{aliceOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

### 403: a USER may only cancel, so alice can't confirm even her own order
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{aliceOrderId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "CONFIRMED" }

### 403: deleting is for ADMIN only
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{aliceOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

# --- Lifecycle and concurrency (ADR 0004) ---

### 409: PENDING can't skip to SHIPPED
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{aliceOrderId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "SHIPPED" }

### 412: If-Match names a version other than the current one
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{aliceOrderId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "7"

{ "status": "CONFIRMED" }

# --- Validation: the gateway checks bodies against the OpenAPI schema; the function the rest (ADR 0007) ---

### 400 from the gateway: an unknown field (the total is always computed by the API)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "currency": "EUR", "totalAmount": 1, "items": [ { "sku": "ABC-123", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 1999 } ] }

### 400 from the gateway: quantity out of range, currency not allowed
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "currency": "CHF", "items": [ { "sku": "ABC-123", "quantity": 0, "unitPrice": 1999 } ] }

### 400 from the function: the same SKU twice, with errors[] pointing at the duplicate
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "currency": "EUR", "items": [ { "sku": "ABC-123", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 1 }, { "sku": "ABC-123", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 1 } ] }

### 415: the body isn't declared as JSON
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: text/plain

currency=EUR

### 400: the order id isn't a UUID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/not-a-uuid
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### 400: list parameters the API doesn't offer, and a limit out of range, in one errors[]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?status=PENDING&limit=1000
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### 404: a path the API doesn't have (a Problem from the gateway, not its default 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
